1. Using Triple Backticks: As mentioned in the GitHub issue, using triple backticks (```) will render code blocks in the Linux Client, but not in the Windows Client. This method seems to be specific to a particular platform and may not be a universal solution.
2. Utilizing UIKit and IModify: RocketChat Apps use UIKit to build rich message blocks. By creating a new file, initiatorMessage.ts in the lib directory, you can use the IModify interface to send rich messages with interactive UI elements. You can add block elements within messages, such as buttons or other clickable elements.
