## Step-by-Step Guide to Adding Code Blocks
1. Create a new file: Initiate by creating a new file named initiatorMessage.ts inside a lib directory in your RocketChat app structure.
2. Use IModify to send rich messages: Utilize the IModify interface to enhance your messages with interactive elements. Access the BlockBuilder class using getBlockBuilder() and start adding block elements within your messages.
3. Add block elements: Specifically, you can use block.addActionsBlock to include interactive buttons or other elements. Provide a unique blockId and define the elements within an array.
4. Define button elements: For each button, you can use blocknewButtonElement to configure its properties. Specify the actionId, text, value, and style for each button. You can also use blocknewPlainTextObject to set the text for the button.
5. Send the message: After configuring your message with the desired block elements, use getCreator().finish(greetBuilder) to send the message to the channel.

By following these steps, you should be able to add code blocks or any other interactive UI components to your messages in the RocketChat web client. Remember to adapt the code examples provided earlier to fit your specific use case and requirements.

